\ ==== fill-polygons ( xs ys faces fills outlines -- ), offline ====

\ fill-polygons draws polygons in the order given: each filled in its own
\ packed colour, every pixel whose centre lies inside by the even-odd rule,
\ so a polygon need not be convex, then outlined in another colour, corner to
\ corner and back to the first, the lines cut to the canvas; an outline
\ below 0 is left out, and so is a polygon with a corner whose coordinate
\ is not finite. xs and ys hold the corners' coordinates; each polygon is
\ an array of indices into them. Drawing needs no window, so
\ capture-bitmap reads the canvas back.

: show-rows ( bitmap -- )
	| bitmap |
	bitmap dim to n-columns to n-rows
	0 n-rows 1 do row
		"" 0 n-columns 1 do column
			bitmap row column @i,j to pixel
			pixel 0 = if "." else pixel 0xff0000 = if "r" else pixel 0x00ff00 = if "g" else "#" then then then +
		loop . cr
	loop ;

: blank ( -- ) 0 ink 0 0 12 12 fill-rect ;

\ === a square filled, no outline: the pixels whose centres lie inside, 0 to 5 each way ===
blank
[ 0 6 6 0 ] vector [ 0 0 6 6 ] vector [ [ 0 1 2 3 ] ] [ 0xffffff ] vector [ -1 ] vector fill-polygons
0 0 7 7 capture-bitmap show-rows
\ ######.
\ ######.
\ ######.
\ ######.
\ ######.
\ ######.
\ .......
clear

\ === a polygon not convex, a notch cut up into its lower edge: rows 2 to 5 filled on either side of it ===
blank
[ 0 6 6 4 4 2 2 0 ] vector [ 0 0 6 6 2 2 6 6 ] vector [ [ 0 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 ] ] [ 0xffffff ] vector [ -1 ] vector fill-polygons
0 0 7 7 capture-bitmap show-rows
\ ######.
\ ######.
\ ##..##.
\ ##..##.
\ ##..##.
\ ##..##.
\ .......
clear

\ === filled green, outlined red: the outline drawn over the fill along the corners ===
blank
[ 1 5 5 1 ] vector [ 1 1 5 5 ] vector [ [ 0 1 2 3 ] ] [ 0x00ff00 ] vector [ 0xff0000 ] vector fill-polygons
0 0 7 7 capture-bitmap show-rows
\ .......
\ .rrrrr.
\ .rgggr.
\ .rgggr.
\ .rgggr.
\ .rrrrr.
\ .......
clear

\ === in order: the second polygon, red, drawn over the first, green ===
blank
[ 0 4 4 0 2 6 6 2 ] vector [ 0 0 4 4 2 2 6 6 ] vector [ [ 0 1 2 3 ] [ 4 5 6 7 ] ]
[ 0x00ff00 0xff0000 ] vector [ -1 -1 ] vector fill-polygons
0 0 7 7 capture-bitmap show-rows
\ gggg...
\ gggg...
\ ggrrrr.
\ ggrrrr.
\ ..rrrr.
\ ..rrrr.
\ .......
clear

\ === a polygon with a corner not finite left out; the other, corners (0,4) (4,4) (4,0), drawn: row 0's centre, y 0.5, meets its long edge at x 3.5, so pixel 3 ===
blank
[ 0 4 null 0 4 4 ] vector [ 0 0 4 4 4 0 ] vector [ [ 0 1 2 ] [ 3 4 5 ] ]
[ 0xff0000 0x00ff00 ] vector [ -1 -1 ] vector fill-polygons
0 0 5 5 capture-bitmap show-rows
\ ...g.
\ ..gg.
\ .ggg.
\ gggg.
\ .....
clear

\ === an outline running far off the canvas cut to it: only the part on the canvas drawn ===
blank
[ -100000 100000 0 ] vector [ 2 2 -100000 ] vector [ [ 0 1 2 ] ] [ 0 ] vector [ 0xff0000 ] vector fill-polygons
0 0 6 4 capture-bitmap show-rows
\ ......
\ ......
\ rrrrrr
\ ......
clear

\ === errors ===
[ 0 1 ] vector [ 0 ] vector [ ] [ ] vector [ ] vector fill-polygons                    \ (as many ys as xs needed)
[ 0 1 ] vector [ 0 1 ] vector [ [ 0 1 ] ] [ ] vector [ -1 ] vector fill-polygons       \ (a fill colour for each face)
[ 0 1 ] vector [ 0 1 ] vector [ [ 0 2 ] ] [ 0 ] vector [ -1 ] vector fill-polygons     \ (a corner index past the points)
[ 0 1 ] vector [ 0 1 ] vector [ 7 ] [ 0 ] vector [ -1 ] vector fill-polygons           \ (a face that is not an array)
[ 0 1 ] vector [ 0 1 ] vector [ ] [ ] vector fill-polygons                             \ (too few operands)
